WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:06.370
in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen."

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:13.610
The reading from the Sinhaxadion for June 30th, on which we commemorate the synaxes of

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:19.090
the Holy Glorious and all-lotted Twelve Apostles.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:24.050
On the 30th of the month we celebrate the synaxes of the Twelve Holy Glorious and Illustrious

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:26.050
Apostles.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:31.530
On this day, illumined by the reflected glory of the first two leaders of the Apostles,

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:37.490
the Church associates the other illustrious Apostles of the Lord, who form a new choir

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:41.010
of shining stars in the spiritual firmament.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:46.210
Foundations and pillars of the Church, they are also the angels who guard the Twelve Gates

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.490
giving access to the heavenly Jerusalem.

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:54.850
The earliest of the people of Israel, the sons of Jacob, were twelve in number, and the

00:00:54.850 --> 00:01:01.570
Lord also chose twelve disciples whom He made witnesses of His teaching and miracles,

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:08.290
whom He sent to preach the kingdom of God, and on whom He conferred the power to cast out

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:12.890
demons and to heal every infirmity.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:18.970
After the resurrection, He sent them throughout the world to proclaim the gospel to the whole

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:25.450
creation, and to baptize all peoples in the name of the Father and of the Son and

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:28.090
of the Holy Spirit.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:33.730
Just as the Son had been sent by the Father into the world for our salvation, so choosing

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:39.730
His disciples and gathering them together, He sent them to proclaim that the kingdom

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:47.770
of heaven was very near, as the Father has sent me, so I send you.

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:55.370
As the condition for becoming His apostles, He asked them to renounce all earthly attachments.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:02:02.970
Provide neither gold nor silver nor brass in your purses nor script for your journey nor

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:08.170
two coats, neither shoes nor yet staves.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:13.890
He also warned them that they would undergo tribulations and persecutions in bearing witness

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:14.890
to Him.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:20.490
Behold, I send you forth as sheep in the midst of wolves.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:24.130
You will be hated by all on account of me.

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:28.530
You will bear witness before governors and kings for my sake.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:35.450
To bear witness to me, but when they deliver you up, take no thought how or what ye shall

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:39.810
speak, or what you are to say.

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:44.810
For it shall be given you in that same hour what ye shall speak.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:52.090
For it is not ye that speak, but the Spirit of your Father which speaketh in you.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:57.370
Witnesses of the resurrection of the Lord, both by their lives and their preaching, the

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:03.730
Holy Apostles offered themselves as a spectacle before the world, before angels and before the

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.610
human race.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:12.850
Starting with St. Paul, we have become a spectacle unto the world, ill-treated, homeless,

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:20.850
naked, we both hunger and thirst, and endure harassment of every kind, rejected by all.

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:26.890
So that by their sacrifice the church might be built on the power of God and not on human

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:34.810
strength, today the Holy and illustrious Apostles form a harmonious choir around the first

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.810
two Apostles.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:43.050
Andrew, the first called Brother of Peter, who proclaimed the gospel in the coastal regions

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:49.930
of Bethinia, Pontus, and Armenia, returning by way of Pontus and Byzantium, he traveled

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:55.810
as far as Greece where he was crucified at Patras in Achaea.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:04:01.850
James, the son of Zebedee, who witnessed to the resurrection throughout the whole of Judea,

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:07.210
he perished by the sword on the orders of King Herod Agrippa, who was jealous of his

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:08.210
renown.

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:14.810
John the Theologian, the brother of James, who rested on the Lord's breast.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:21.130
After having proclaimed Christ in the province of Asia, he was exiled to Patmos on the orders

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:26.250
of Domitian, where he wrote the gospel and the apocalypse.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:33.130
He finally returned to Ephesus, where he fell asleep in peace at a great age.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:39.810
Philip, who came from Bethsida in Galilee like Peter and Andrew, he proclaimed the good news

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:46.370
in the province of Asia and in the region of Yerapulis in Fridia, in the company of his sister

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:54.530
Mariamne and of Saint Bartholomew, he died in Yerapulis being crucified by the pagans.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:05:02.210
Thomas, also called Didymus, who spread the gospel among the Parthians, Meeds, and Persians,

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:04.810
and the inhabitants of India.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:08.690
He was pierced to death by pagan lances.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:15.330
Bartholomew preached in Lydia and in Misia, along with the Apostle Philip.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:21.930
After the death of the latter, he continued his mission in Arabia Felix, now North Yemen,

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:28.250
in Persia, and in India, and finished his course in Armenia, where he was crucified

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:32.530
in Albanapulis, or Urbanapulis.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:41.330
His body was placed in a lead box and thrown into the sea, but was later recovered in Sicily.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:48.810
Matthew, the publican, formerly called Levi, was the brother of James the son of Alphius.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:53.890
After having written his gospel, he left on a mission to the Parthenians.

00:05:53.890 --> 00:06:00.930
It is said that he was burned alive in Yerapulis, on the banks of the Euphrates.

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:08.890
James, the son of Alphius, proclaimed Christ in Gaza, and in and around the Leltheriopolis.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:14.170
He was crucified in the town of Ostrasin in Egypt.

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:20.410
Simon the zealot, from Cana and Galilee, who is also called Nathaniel in the Gospel

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:26.410
of John, proclaimed the good news in Mauritania, in North Africa.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:32.210
It is said that he then left for Great Britain, where he was crucified.

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:40.130
Jude, a kinsman of the Lord, also called Thaddeus, and Levi by Saint Matthew, departed on

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:46.850
a mission to Mesopotamia and finished his days in the region near Mount Ararat, where he

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:51.410
was hanged and pierced with arrows by pagans.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:59.130
Matthias was added to the number of the apostles after the ascension to replace Judas the traitor.

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:05.090
He preached the gospel in Ethiopia where he gave his soul into God's hands after suffering

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:09.130
numerous tortures at the hands of the pagans.

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:15.550
It is the custom to associate the holy evangelists with these blessed apostles, Mark, a spiritual

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:21.730
son of Saint Peter, who evangelized Alexandria and the Pentopolis, and who suffered martyrdom

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:24.730
by being crushed under the weight of a rock.

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:31.330
Luke, the physician, and first iconographer, who after having accompanied Saint Paul on his

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:36.010
journeys, wrote his gospel under the apostles' influence.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:43.010
Finally, settling in Thebes in Boatia, he died there in peace at the age of 84.

00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:51.530
It is on the testimony of these holy apostles whose sound is gone out into all lands in order

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:58.250
to proclaim the reality of Christ's resurrection that the church has been built.

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:04.450
If they occupy the first place in the assembly of the saints, it is precisely because detaching

00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:11.570
themselves from everything else in order to follow the Lord, they became His perfect imitators

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:19.410
and proclaimed to all, be ye followers of us, just as we are of Him.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:25.810
Once the generation of those who had known the Lord during His earthly life had passed,

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:34.410
the Apostolic ministry did not end, but as Saint Paul testifies, was transmitted to all those

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:41.690
who have beheld the resurrection of Christ through the illumination of the Holy Spirit.

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:47.690
The grace of the Apostolic Charisma is not limited to the oral proclamation of the good news,

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:55.170
but is shared by all the saints who have contributed to the building up of the church through their

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:59.130
witness to the resurrection.

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:06.130
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us and save us.
